  ((select id from public.curriculum_doc where doc_key = $txt$SK-MATH-1-8$txt$), (select id from public.strand where doc_id = (select id from public.curriculum_doc where doc_key = $txt$SK-MATH-1-8$txt$) and code = $txt$N$txt$), 1, $txt$N1.9$txt$, $txt$official$txt$, null, $txt$outcome$txt$, null, $txt$Demonstrate an understanding of addition of numbers with answers to 20 and the corresponding subtraction facts, concretely, pictorially, physically, and symbolically by: using familiar and mathematical language to describe additive and subtractive actions from their experience; creating and solving problems in context that involve addition and subtraction; modelling addition and subtraction using a variety of concrete and visual representations, and recording the process symbolically.$txt$, $txt${"processes":"C, CN, ME, PS, R, V","note":"List items from the official page are joined with \"; \". Process tags moved to processes."}$txt$::jsonb, $txt$https://curriculum.gov.sk.ca/CurriculumOutcomeContent?id=145&oc=78108$txt$, 9, false, $txt$2026-10-17$txt$::date),
  ((select id from public.curriculum_doc where doc_key = $txt$SK-MATH-1-8$txt$), (select id from public.strand where doc_id = (select id from public.curriculum_doc where doc_key = $txt$SK-MATH-1-8$txt$) and code = $txt$N$txt$), 1, $txt$N1.10$txt$, $txt$official$txt$, null, $txt$outcome$txt$, null, $txt$Describe and use mental mathematics strategies (memorization not intended), such as: counting on and counting back; making 10; doubles; using addition to subtract; to determine basic addition facts to 18 and related subtraction facts.$txt$, $txt${"processes":"C, CN, ME, PS, R, V","note":"List items from the official page are joined with \"; \". Process tags moved to processes."}$txt$::jsonb, $txt$https://curriculum.gov.sk.ca/CurriculumOutcomeContent?id=145&oc=78116$txt$, 10, false, $txt$2026-10-17$txt$::date),
  ((select id from public.curriculum_doc where doc_key = $txt$SK-MATH-1-8$txt$), (select id from public.strand where doc_id = (select id from public.curriculum_doc where doc_key = $txt$SK-MATH-1-8$txt$) and code = $txt$P$txt$), 1, $txt$P1.1$txt$, $txt$official$txt$, null, $txt$outcome$txt$, null, $txt$Demonstrate an understanding of repeating patterns (two to four elements) by: describing; reproducing; extending; creating patterns using manipulatives, diagrams, sounds, and actions.$txt$, $txt${"processes":"C, PS, R, V","note":"List items from the official page are joined with \"; \". Process tags moved to processes."}$txt$::jsonb, $txt$https://curriculum.gov.sk.ca/CurriculumOutcomeContent?id=145&oc=78122$txt$, 11, false, $txt$2026-10-17$txt$::date),
